You don't need an Alpha to compile setnetbootinfo. At least the way I
installed my Multia was by using a setnetbootinfo compiled on an i386. Just
add -I/sys/arch/alpha for stand/common/bbinfo.h .

>From there, it is pretty straightforward.

> In short...help!! Someone mentioned a jumper. I can't find such in the 
> docs other than as described above. I don't have another Alpha (or for 
> that matter another NetBSD box) to play with so I can't patch the boot
> loader. I welcome any input.

The jumper mentioned is for enabling fail-safe mode, for reverting to
known good firmware in case of flash corruption. It is located on the
bottom side of the system board and is marked W7/W11.


